{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]She's got a smile that it seems to me
[C]Reminds me of childhood memories
Where [G]everything
Was as fresh as a bright blue [D]sky
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Now and then when I see her face
She takes me away to that special place
And if I stared to long
I'd probably break down and cry
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Whoa Oh, Sweet [C]child o' mine[D]
[A]Whoa, Oh, Oh, Oh [C]Sweet love o' [D]mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Solo Break}
She's got eyes of the bluest skies
As if they thought of rain
I hate to look into those eyes
And see an ounce of pain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Her hair reminds me of a warm safe place
Where as a child I'd hide
And pray for the thunder and rain
To quietly pass me by
{end_of_verse}

